  "stakes": {
    "do": "Buy rope, casks, wax and boots at yard prices instead of town prices. Put a load on Marisol Vasquez's line and watch it hold or part.",
    "lose": "A cheap line breaks under real weight and takes cattle or a hand with it. The cheaper rival's rope is what is stacked in front.",
    "decide": "Whether to buy Marisol's rope at her price or the undercutter's, and whether Naomi Freeman or Orin Teague gets the outfit's ironwork."
  },
  "art_gap": "Reads as a fenced yard with camp props. Needs a rope walk, stacked barrels, a forge and a hide rack. Four Griffin-assigned trades were grouped here for room, per ECONOMY.md's own note that the Griffin cluster is movable."
}
